      "question": "Two triangles have all corresponding sides equal. What can we conclude?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "They are similar",
        "B": "They are congruent",
        "C": "They are isosceles",
        "D": "They have equal areas only",
        "E": "Nothing can be concluded"
      },
      "answer": "B",
      "explanation": "SSS (Side-Side-Side) congruence: if all three sides are equal, triangles are congruent.",
      "steps": [
        "1. All corresponding sides equal.",
        "2. Apply SSS congruence theorem.",
        "3. Triangles are congruent."
      ],
      "fastStrategy": "SSS: three sides equal ⇒ congruent triangles."
